WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.080
NARRATOR: Invented
in Holland in 1898,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.270
the deli slicer
launched a revolution

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.220
behind the meat counter.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.500
No longer was it
necessary to carve meats

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.020
and cheeses entirely by hand.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.570
With a turn of a crank,
the deli slicer produced

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.130
precise cuts in a jiffy.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.390
The modern deli slicer is
powered by electricity,

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.270
with a manual override for
the carriage that delivers

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.455
food to a spinning blade.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.010
Production begins with
a cast aluminum base.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.110
A worker installs
a cam mechanism

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.940
that is part of a
system for adjusting

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.035
the thickness of the slice.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.940
He threads wiring, connected
to an on/off indicator light

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.200
through holes in the base.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.400
Then he screws an index
knob onto the shaft,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.815
protruding from the cam
mechanism installed earlier.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.375
An important warning
label comes next.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.420
Then, he seals the gap around
the blade shaft with silicone

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.550
and removes the excess
with soapy water.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.660
Next up is the wiring
for the slicer motor.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.040
She clamps the wires
together and bolts the clamps

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.720
to the inside of
the aluminum base.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.835
She inserts the on/off
switch and the plastic trim.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.660
Then attaches a
device that will slide

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.750
to adjust the gap between the
gauge plate and the blade.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.060
Thereby, controlling the
thickness of the cut.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.640
The deli slicer is
ready for the slide rod

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.980
and carriage sub assembly
that will deliver

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.270
food to the spinning blade.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.020
The carriage will
move across a track

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.255
that she now attaches
to the lip of the base.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.015
She tests the carriage assembly
to confirm that it's on track.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.250
The next worker
secures the blade motor

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.615
to the wiring with bolts.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:19.630
He connects the motor to the
blade shaft with a drive belt.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.210
Operating the motor allows
him to observe the drive

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.730
belt and pulleys in
action, confirming

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:25.885
that they operate smoothly.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.120
Once the gauge
plate is installed,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.755
they move on to
making the blade.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.300
Computer guided cutters
sloped to steel surface

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.685
and carve a precise
bevel onto the rim.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.840
It goes from a rough
blank to a precisely

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.445
shaped blade in just minutes.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.050
The next worker etches the
company logo and production

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.205
date into the blade metal.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.160
Another lathe
pre-sharpens the blade

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.620
to the point where it could
cut through something as fine

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.450
as several thousands of an inch.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.020
A worker slides the blade
onto the drive shaft

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.090
and secures it in
place with a nut.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.100
He now checks the alignment
of the gauge plate in relation

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.420
to the blade.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.330
He turns the thickness
mechanism to close the gap

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.220
and checks it again.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.950
With a dial indicator, he
measures the position of

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.930
the blade even more precisely.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.200
This tool confirms that the
blade is in the exact position

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.030
for cutting and
that it won't lose

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.580
that position once activated.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.980
This deli slicer comes
with its own sharpening

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.665
system, a grinding wheel,
and protective casing.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.640
He mounts the grinder
and activates it to hone

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.650
the edge to razor sharpness.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.590
When the blade cuts through
tissue paper cleanly,

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.600
it's ready for real
slicing action.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.220
A worker screws the arm for the
sliding tray to the carriage.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.510
He uses a spacer
disk to establish

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.300
the correct distance between
the food tray and the blade.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.140
He sets the food tray on
the arm and checks the gap

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.325
between it and the blade.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.870
Once the two are correctly
aligned, he removes the spacer

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.865
and latches the safety
guard to the blade.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:30.190
And now for a test, verifying
that the tray doesn't drag or

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.570
scrape against the blade guard.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.450
Below, they've installed rods to
move the carriage on the track.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.550
The system can be
manually operated

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.950
or driven by a second motor.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.830
Finally, a worker cleans
the slicing machine

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:45.670
until it gleams.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:51.370
At 135 pounds, this deli
slicer is no lightweight.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.235
So they use a crane to lower
it into the packing box.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.900
Hefty and heavy duty,
this deli slicer

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.970
should have what it takes to
cut it at the meat market.

